course: dictionary
lesson: 5120
title: Who are the Inuit?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The Inuit are Indigenous peoples who live in the Arctic, the cold northern lands of Canada, Greenland, Alaska and nearby. «The Inuit of the Arctic hunted seals and whales, used kayaks and dog sleds, and in winter some built snow houses called igloos.» These clues tell you they adapted to a very cold place.
explain: Inuit can also be an adjective, a describing word. «Inuit languages build long words from parts.» Here Inuit means of or about these peoples and their languages. Ask yourself: is the word naming a group of people, or describing something that belongs to them?
explain: One person is an Inuk. The people together are the Inuit, and the word Inuit does not change in the plural. Some words from Inuit languages are now used in English too, such as kayak and igloo, so you may already know them.
fact: Inuit are Indigenous peoples of the Arctic regions of Canada, Greenland and Alaska.
fact: Inuit (adjective) means of or about these peoples and their cultures and languages.
fact: «The Inuit of the Arctic hunted seals and whales, used kayaks and dog sleds.»
fact: Kayak and igloo are words that come from Inuit languages.
fact: Most Inuit today live in modern towns, and Nunavut, a Canadian territory, is largely Inuit.
exercise: «The Inuit of the Arctic hunted seals and whales.» Where did the Inuit live? | On the Pacific islands near Australia | In the hot deserts of Africa | In the high mountains of Peru | *In the cold Arctic lands of Canada, Greenland and Alaska
exercise: «Inuit languages build long words from parts.» What does Inuit mean in this sentence? | A cold, windy place | *Of or about the Inuit peoples | A type of boat | The name of a country
exercise: What is one person of the Inuit called? | *An Inuk | An igloo | A kayak | An Inuit
test: «In winter some built snow houses called igloos.» Which word in this sentence names a winter shelter? | *Igloos | Winter | Built | Snow
test: Which of these words came from an Inuit language? | Bicycle | *Kayak | Cricket | Tennis
exam: In the sentence «The Inuit live in the Arctic», what does Inuit mean? | A kind of snow house | A type of sled | A cold wind from the north | *The Indigenous peoples of the Arctic
